\ Information                                                                                                                   Conversion utility for KIM-1 and SYM-1 format tapes.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ Load - main screen                                            empty  forth definitions  decimal                               application  warning on                                                                                                         : TITLE ." KIMTAPE version 0.5  17-May-04" cr ;                                                                                 cr .( Compiling: )  title  2 load                                                                                               cr .( Save to disk? )  y/n                                      [if]  turnkey program  KIMTAPE.COM  [then]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ Load - defers                                                 defer ?BREAK  ' noop is ?break      \ user break check          defer SET-IO  ' noop is set-io      \ set console method        defer ERRFIX  ' noop is errfix      \ on error handler                                                                          3 load      \ load electives and application                                                                                     ' (?break) is ?break          \ enable user break               ' dos-io is set-io            \ enable console redirection     \ ' deloutfile +defer errfix    \ delete outfile on error       \ wrtchk off                    \ disable overwrite check                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \ Load - electives and application                               4 5 thru                       \ error handler                  6 load                         \ number output                  7 load                         \ basic strings                 \ 8 load                         \ extra strings                 9 14 thru                      \ command-line parsing           15 17 thru                     \ file primitives                18 23 thru                     \ default files                  24 load                        \ buffered input file            25 load                        \ buffered output file           30 #screens 1- thru            \ application                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ Error handler - +DEFER ?THROW ?CATCH                          system                                                          \ Append a new behaviour to an existing deferred word           : +DEFER  ( xt <name> -- )  >r  :noname  r> compile,              ' >body dup @ compile,  >r  postpone ;  r> ! ;                application                                                                                                                     \ THROW exception code n if flag is non-zero                    : ?THROW  ( flag n -- )  swap 0<> and throw ;                                                                                   \ Perform CATCH intercepting exception code n only              : ?CATCH  ( xt n -- n )  >r catch dup r> <> over and throw ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ Error handler - ERROR1 ERROR2 ESC= ESCKEY? (?BREAK)           \ Quit to DOS with no msg and return code = 1                   : ERROR1  ( -- )  abort ;                                                                                                       \ Quit with abort msg                                           : ERROR2  ( -- )  ."  ... aborting"  error1 ;                                                                                   \ Test char for ESC or Ctrl-C                                   : ESC=  ( char -- flag )  dup 27 =  swap 3 =  or ;                                                                              \ Check if ESC or Ctrl-C key was pressed                        : ESCKEY?  ( -- flag )  0  key? if  key esc=  or  then ;                                                                        \ Check user break                                              : (?BREAK)  ( -- )  esckey? if  beep cr                           ." User break - exit program? " y/n if  error2  then  then ;  \ Number output -                                               : (UD.) ( ud -- addr u )  <# #s #> ;                            : (U.)  ( u  -- addr u )  0 (d.) ;                              : (.)   ( n  -- addr u )  s>d (d.) ;                            : UD.   ( ud -- )  (ud.) type space ;                           : UD.R  ( ud n -- )  >r (ud.) r> over - spaces type ;                                                                           : (DH.) ( ud -- addr u )                                          base @ >r hex <# 8 0 do # loop #> r> base ! ;                 : (H.)  ( u -- addr u )  0 (dh.) 4 /string ;                    : (HB.) ( u -- addr u )  (h.) 2 /string ;                       : DH.   ( ud -- )  (dh.) type space ;                           : H.    ( u -- )  (h.) type space ;                             : HB.   ( u -- )  (hb.) type space ;                                                                                                                                                            \ Strings - SPLIT STRING+C C/STRING STRING/                     \ Split string at character leaving first on top                : SPLIT  ( a u char -- a2 u2 a3 u3 )                              >r 2dup r> scan 2swap 2 pick - ;                                                                                              \ Append character to end of string                             : STRING+C  ( a u char -- a2 u2 )  >r 2dup + r> swap c! 1+ ;                                                                    \ Extract character from start of string                        : C/STRING  ( a u -- a2 u2 char )  over >r 1 /string r> c@ ;                                                                    \ Return n right-most characters of string                      : STRING/  ( a u n -- a2 u2 )  over min over swap - /string ;                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ Strings - S= S+ STRING S!                                     \ Compare two strings for equality                              : S=  ( a1 u1 a2 u2 -- flag )  compare 0= ;                                                                                     255 ( buffer size ) local %1  dup , allot                                                                                       \ Concatenate two strings placing result in temp buffer         : S+  ( a1 u1 a2 u2 -- a3 u3 )  2>r  %1 @ min  %1 cell+ 0         2swap string+  %1 @  over -  2r> rot min  string+ ;                                                                           \ Define string variable with max length u                      -? : STRING  create ( u -- ) 255 min dup c, 0 c, allot            does> ( -- a u ) 1+ count ;                                                                                                   \ Store string a u to string variable                           : S!  ( a u sa su -- )  drop  1- dup >r  1- c@ min  r> place ;  \ Cmdline parsing - ARGC ARGV                                   create ARGC  ( -- a )                                             1 cells allot ( item# )  2 cells allot ( string )               argc 3 cells erase                                                                                                            \ Parse next string  ARGC OFF resets                            : ARGV  ( -- a u -1 | 0 )                                         1 argc +!                                                       argc cell+ 2@  0 0                                              argc @  0 ?do                                                     2drop  bl skip  bl split                                      loop  2swap 2drop                                               dup if  -1  else  and  then ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ Cmdline parsing - BADOPTION /NUM /HEXNUM /NUMRANGE            : BADOPTION  ( -- )  cr ." Invalid option"  error2 ;                                                                            \ Parse number n from string                                    : /NUM  ( a u -- 0 0 n )  number?                                 if  drop  else  badoption  then  0 0 ( stop parsing) rot ;                                                                    \ Parse hex number n from string                                : /HEXNUM  ( a u -- 0 0 n )  base @ >r  hex /num  r> base ! ;                                                                   \ As for /NUM but checks n3 is in the range n1 to n2            : /NUMRANGE  ( a u n1 n2 -- 0 0 n3 )                              2>r /num  dup  2r> 1+  within  0= if badoption then ;                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ Cmdline parsing - SETOPTION                                   \ Process each character in a switch option string              defer SETOPTION  ( a u char -- a u )  ' drop is setoption                                                                       exit                                                                                                                            \ Example of use                                                : (SETOPTION)  ( a u char -- a u )                                upcase [char] A = if  A-variable on  else  badoption  then ;                                                                  ' (setoption) is setoption                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ Cmdline parsing - PARSEOPTION                                 \ Parse multiple switch options from the command-line           : PARSEOPTION  ( -- )                                             begin                                                             argv                                                          while  ( not end )                                                c/string                                                        dup [char] / =  swap [char] - =  or if ( switch )                 begin  dup                                                      while  c/string setoption                                       repeat  2drop                                                 else                                                              2drop  -1 argc +! ( backup )  exit                            then                                                          repeat ;                                                                                                                      \ Cmdline parsing - PARSEFILENAME                               \ Parse one or more strings/filenames from the command-line     defer PARSEFILENAME  ( -- )  ' noop is parsefilename                                                                            exit                                                                                                                            \ Example of use                                                : (PARSEFILENAME)  ( -- )                                         argv 0= if ." no filename specified"  error1  then              64 min infile place ;                                                                                                         ' (parsefilename) is parsefilename                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \ Cmdline parsing - CMD! CMD@ PARSECMD                          \ Set command string for parsing                                : CMD!  ( a u -- )  argc cell+ 2!  argc off ;                                                                                   \ Get command-line string                                       : CMD@  ( -- a u )  128 count ;                                                                                                 \ Parse command-line setting options/filenames                  : PARSECMD  ( -- )                                                cmd@ cmd!  parseoption  parsefilename ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \ File primitives - ?FERROR                                     \ Display msg and abort on file error                           : ?FERROR  ( ior n -- )                                           swap if                                                           cr ." File "  case                                                3  of  ." read"  endof                                          4  of  ." write"  endof                                         5  of  ." position"  endof                                      6  of  ." size"  endof                                        endcase                                                         ."  error"  error2                                            else  drop  then ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ File primitives - READF WRITEF READL WRITEL                   \ Read binary                                                   : READF  ( a u handle -- a u2 )                                   ?break  >r over swap r>  read-file  3 ?ferror ;                                                                               \ Write binary                                                  : WRITEF  ( a u handle -- )                                       ?break  write-file  4 ?ferror ;                                                                                               \ Read text  flag=0 if end-of-file                              : READL  ( a u handle -- a u2 flag )                              ?break  >r over swap r>  read-line  3 ?ferror ;                                                                               \ Write text                                                    : WRITEL  ( a u handle -- )                                       ?break  write-line  4 ?ferror ;                               \ File primitives - FPOS REPOSF FSIZE RESIZEF                   \ File position                                                 : FPOS  ( handle  -- ud )  file-position  5 ?ferror ;                                                                           \ Reposition file                                               : REPOSF  ( ud handle  -- )  reposition-file  5 ?ferror ;                                                                       \ File size                                                     : FSIZE  ( handle  -- ud )  file-size  6 ?ferror ;                                                                              \ Resize file                                                   : RESIZEF  ( ud handle  -- )  resize-file  6 ?ferror ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \ Default files -                                               create   INFILE   65 allot          \ filename buffer           variable INFID    infid off         \ file ID  0=closed         0 value  INBUF                      \ buffer                    variable INPTR    variable INSIZ    \ pointer, chars in buffer                                                                  create   OUTFILE  65 allot                                      variable OUTFID   outfid off                                    0 value  OUTBUF                                                 variable OUTPTR   variable OUTSIZ                                                                                               variable WRTCHK   wrtchk on         \ file overwrite check                                                                      : RESETINBUF  ( -- )  inbuf inptr !  insiz off ;                : RESETOUTBUF  ( -- )  outbuf outptr !  outsiz off ;                                                                            \ Default files - CLOSEINFILE CLOSEOUTFILE CLOSEFILES           defer (FLUSHWRITE)  ' 0    is (flushwrite)                                                                                      \ Close input file - errors not reported                        : CLOSEINFILE  ( -- )  infid @ ?dup                               if  close-file drop  then  infid off ;                                                                                        \ Close output file - errors not reported                       : CLOSEOUTFILE  ( -- )  outfid @ ?dup                             if  (flushwrite) drop  close-file drop  then  outfid off ;                                                                    \ Close all files - errors not reported                         : CLOSEFILES  ( -- )  closeinfile  closeoutfile ;                                                                               ' closefiles +defer errfix  \ close files on error                                                                              \ Default files - DELOUTFILE REPOSIN/OUTFILE IN/OUTFILEPOS      \ Close and delete output file - errors not reported            : DELOUTFILE  ( -- )  outfid @  closeoutfile                      if  outfile count delete-file drop  then ;                                                                                    \ Reposition input file to position d                           : REPOSINFILE  ( ud -- )  infid @ reposf resetinbuf ;                                                                           \ Reposition output file to position d                          : REPOSOUTFILE  ( ud -- )  (flushwrite) drop  outfid @ reposf ;                                                                 \ Input file position                                           : INFILEPOS  ( -- ud )  infid @ fpos  insiz @  0 d- ;                                                                           \ Output file position                                          : OUTFILEPOS  ( -- ud )  outfid @ fpos  outsiz @  0 d+ ;        \ Default files - OPENINFILE                                    \ Open an input file using file access mode fam                 : OPENINFILE  ( fam -- )                                          infile count  2dup upper  cr ." infile:  "  2dup type           infid off  rot open-file  ?dup if  255 and                        case                                                              2  of  ."  file not found"  endof                               3  of  ."  path not found"  endof                               4  of  ."  too many open files"  endof                          5  of  ."  access denied"  endof                                ."  open error"                                               endcase  error2                                               then  infid !  resetinbuf ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ Default files - OPENOUTFILE                                   \ Create an output file using file access mode fam              : OPENOUTFILE  ( fam -- )                                         outfile count  2dup upper  cr ." outfile: "  2dup type          outfid off  wrtchk @ if                                           2dup r/o open-file  0= if                                         close-file                                                      beep ."  exists - overwrite? "  y/n 0= if error2 then         then  drop                                                    then                                                            rot create-file if  ."  create error"  error2  then             outfid !  resetoutbuf ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \ Default files - READDATA WRITEDATA READTEXT WRITETEXT         \ Read binary from input file                                   : READDATA  ( a u1 -- a u2 )  infid @ readf ;                                                                                   \ Write binary to output file                                   : WRITEDATA  ( a u -- )  outfid @ writef ;                                                                                      \ Read text from input file  flag=0 if end-of-file              : READTEXT  ( a u1 -- a u2 flag )  infid @ readl ;                                                                              \ Write text to output file                                     : WRITETEXT  ( a u -- )  outfid @ writel ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ Buffered input file - REFILLREAD READCHAR                     here to INBUF  1024 allot  resetinbuf                                                                                           \ Refill read buffer                                            : REFILLREAD  ( -- )                                              resetinbuf  inbuf 1024 readdata  insiz !  drop ;                                                                              \ Read char from buffered input file                            \ : READCHAR  ( -- char -1 | 0 )  insiz @ 0= if refillread then \  insiz @ if inptr @ c@ 1 inptr +! -1 insiz +! -1 else 0 then ;                                                                code READCHAR  ( -- char -1 | 0 )  0 # insiz ) cmp                1 l# jnz  c: refillread ;c  1 L:  ax ax sub  ax insiz ) cmp     2 l# jz  inptr ) bx mov  0 [bx] al mov  ax push  inptr ) inc    insiz ) dec  -1 # ax mov  2 L: 1push end-code                                                                                 \ Buffered output file - FLUSHWRITE WRITECHAR                   here to OUTBUF  1024 allot  resetoutbuf                                                                                         \ Flush write buffer                                            :noname  ( -- ior )  outbuf  outsiz @  outfid @  write-file       resetoutbuf ;  is (flushwrite)                                                                                                : FLUSHWRITE  ( -- )  (flushwrite)  4 ?ferror ;                                                                                 \ Write char to buffered output file                            \ : WRITECHAR  ( char -- )  outsiz @ 1024 = if flushwrite then  \  outptr @ c! 1 outptr +! 1 outsiz +! ;                                                                                        code WRITECHAR  ( char -- )  1024 # outsiz ) cmp                  1 l# jnz  c: flushwrite ;c  1 L:  ax pop  outptr ) bx mov       al 0 [bx] mov  outptr ) inc  outsiz ) inc  next  end-code                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ Help screen - HELP                                            : HELP  ( -- )                                                    cr ." Use:  KIMTAPE [options] infile[.typ] [outfile[.typ]]" cr  cr ." -C    console output              -M    make wavefile"    cr ." -Bn   HYPERTAPE speed  2x 3x 6x   -I    invert wavefile"  cr ." -U    SYM-1 high speed format     -V    VOC wavefile"     cr ." -Fn   offset  -127 to 127         -R    RAW wavefile"     cr ." -Hn   hysteresis  0 to 127        -Ln   leader (sec)"     cr ." -Gn   timing  -2 to 2             -T    sine tone"        cr ." -An   load address (hex)          -Dn   prog ID (hex)"    cr                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ Help screen - HELP                                              cr ." default: decode WAV file, KIM-1 format"                   cr ."          load address=0200, file ID=00"                   cr                                                              cr ." Conversion utility for KIM-1 and SYM-1 format audio"      cr ." tapes. Input/output is an 8-bit mono WAV, VOC or RAW"     cr ." wavefile recorded at 22,050 samples per second."          error1 ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ Misc                                                          : M+!  ( n a -- )  dup >r  2@  rot m+  r> 2! ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ Variables -                                                   variable SADDR              \ start address                     variable EADDR              \ end address +1                    variable BITCOUNT           \ bit counter                       variable CHECKSUM           \ checksum                          variable CONOUT             \ console flag                      variable DECODING           \ 0=encode nz=decode                variable FILEID             \ file ID                           variable POLARITY           \ wave polarity  0=normal nz=invert variable LASTCYCLE          \ last cycle weight                 variable LEADTIME           \ leader (secs)                     variable SAMPLECOUNT        \ sample count                      variable SPEED              \ speed                             variable MODE               \ mode flag  0=KIM nz=SYM           variable SINE               \ tone type                         variable WAVE               \ wave type                         \ Variables -                                                   2variable DECODECOUNT       \ bytes decoded                     2variable WAVESIZ           \ wavefile data size                                                                                4  constant EOT             \ Ascii end of text character       22 constant SYNC            \ Ascii sync character                                                                              0   value BIAS              \ waveform DC offset adjust         8   value DATABITS          \ character length                  3   value HYSTERESIS        \ hysteresis level                  7   value MAXWAVE           \ max sample for high tone          130 value SILENCEMAX        \ upper hysteresis level            124 value SILENCEMIN        \ lower hysteresis level                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ SETLEVELS WAVETYPE                                            \ Set waveform trigger levels                                   : SETLEVELS  ( -- )                                               1275  hysteresis 10 *  2dup                                     - 10 / bias +  0 max 255 min  to silencemin                     + 10 / bias +  0 max 255 min  to silencemax ;                                                                                 \ Get default wavefile type                                     : WAVETYPE  ( -- a u )                                            wave @  case                                                      0  of  s" WAV"  endof                                           1  of  s" VOC"  endof                                           2  of  s" RAW"  endof                                         endcase ;                                                                                                                                                                                     \ FLIP-POLARITY SYM?                                            \ Invert polarity flag                                          : FLIP-POLARITY  ( -- )                                           polarity @  0=  polarity ! ;                                                                                                  \ SYM mode test                                                 : SYM?  ( -- flag )                                               mode @ ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ (SETOPTION)                                                   \ Set options                                                   : (SETOPTION)  ( a u char -- a u )                                upcase case                                                       [char] A  of  /hexnum  saddr !  endof                           [char] B  of  2 6 /numrange  speed !  endof                     [char] C  of  conout on  endof                                  [char] D  of  /hexnum  fileid !  endof                          [char] F  of  -127 127 /numrange to bias  setlevels  endof      [char] G  of  -2 2 /numrange  maxwave +  to maxwave  endof      [char] H  of  0 127 /numrange to hysteresis setlevels  endof    [char] I  of  polarity on  endof                                [char] L  of  /num  leadtime !  endof                           [char] M  of  decoding off  endof                               [char] R  of  2 wave !  endof                                   [char] T  of  1 sine !  endof                               \ (SETOPTION)                                                       [char] U  of  mode on  endof                                    [char] V  of  1 wave !  endof                                   badoption  endcase ;                                                                                                        ' (setoption) is setoption                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ (PARSEFILENAME)                                               \ Parse filenames                                               : (PARSEFILENAME)  ( -- )                                         argv  0= if  help  then                                         decoding @ if  wavetype  else  s" PRG"  then                    +filename  64 min  infile place                                 argv  0= if  infile count  -path -filename  then                decoding @ if  s" PRG"  else  wavetype  then                    +filename  64 min  outfile place ;                                                                                            ' (parsefilename) is parsefilename                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \ STR WAV-HDR VOC-HDR                                           \ Define n character string header                              -? : STR  create ( n -- ) c,  does> ( -- a u ) count ;                                                                          hex                                                             2C str WAV-HDR  ( WAV header )                                  4952 , 4646 , 0000 , 0000 , 4157 , 4556 , 6D66 , 2074 ,         0010 , 0000 , 0001 , 0001 , 5622 , 0000 , 5622 , 0000 ,         0001 , 0008 , 6164 , 6174 , 0000 , 0000 ,                                                                                       20 str VOC-HDR  ( VOC header )                                  7243 , 6165 , 6974 , 6576 , 5620 , 696F , 6563 , 4620 ,         6C69 , 1A65 , 001A , 010A , 1129 , 0001 , 0000 , 00D3 ,         decimal                                                                                                                                                                                         \ 0BIT-SQR-KIM 1BIT-SQR-KIM                                     hex                                                             9 str 0BIT-SQR-KIM  ( 1 1/2 cycle 3600 hz - square equalized )  ( normal )                                                      DC8C , 73FF , 0023 , DC8C , FF c,                               ( inverted )                                                    2373 , 8C00 , FFDC , 2373 , 00 c,                                                                                               9 str 1BIT-SQR-KIM  ( 1 cycle 2400 hz - square equalized )      ( normal )                                                      DC9D , FFF5 , 5597 , 112B , 00 c,                               ( inverted )                                                    2362 , 000A , AA68 , EED4 , FF c,                               decimal                                                                                                                                                                                         \ 0BIT-SIN-KIM 1BIT-SIN-KIM                                     hex                                                             9 str 0BIT-SIN-KIM  ( 1 1/2 cycle 3600 hz - sine )              ( normal )                                                      FFBE , 41BE , 4100 , FFBE , BE c,                               ( inverted )                                                    0041 , BE41 , BEFF , 0041 , 41 c,                                                                                               9 str 1BIT-SIN-KIM  ( 1 cycle 2400 hz - sine )                  ( normal )                                                      FED2 , ACEF , 1154 , 2E02 , 80 c,                               ( inverted )                                                    012D , 5310 , EEAB , D1FD , 7F c,                               decimal                                                                                                                                                                                         \ 0BIT-SQR-SYM 1BIT-SQR-SYM                                     hex                                                             10 str 0BIT-SQR-SYM  ( 1/2 cycle 700 hz - square equalized )    ( normal )                                                      C79F , EEDE , FFF8 , FFFF , FFFF , FFFF , FFFF , FFFF ,         ( inverted )                                                    3960 , 1121 , 0007 , 0000 , 0000 , 0000 , 0000 , 0000 ,                                                                         10 str 1BIT-SQR-SYM  ( 1 cycle 1400 hz - square equalized )     ( normal )                                                      C79F , EEDE , FFF8 , 3960 , 1121 , 0007 , 0000 , 0000 ,         ( inverted )                                                    3960 , 1121 , 0007 , C79F , EEDE , FFF8 , FFFF , FFFF ,         decimal                                                                                                                                                                                         \ 0BIT-SIN-SYM 1BIT-SIN-SYM                                     hex                                                             10 str 0BIT-SIN-SYM  ( 1/2 cycle 700 hz - sine )                ( normal )                                                      AE97 , D5C3 , F2E5 , FFFA , FAFF , E5F2 , C3D5 , 97AE ,         ( inverted )                                                    5168 , 2A3C , 0D1A , 0005 , 0500 , 1A0D , 3C2A , 6851 ,                                                                         10 str 1BIT-SIN-SYM  ( 1 cycle 1400 hz - sine )                 ( normal )                                                      E3B7 , FCFC , B7E3 , 3A5B , 0B1F , 0101 , 1F0B , 5B3A ,         ( inverted )                                                    1C48 , 0303 , 481C , C5A4 , F4E0 , FEFE , E0F4 , A4C5 ,         decimal                                                                                                                                                                                         \ 0BIT-SQR 1BIT-SQR 0BIT-SIN 1BIT-SIN SENDBIT                   \ Bit data                                                      defer 0BIT-SQR  ( a u -- )                                      defer 1BIT-SQR  ( a u -- )                                      defer 0BIT-SIN  ( a u -- )                                      defer 1BIT-SIN  ( a u -- )                                                                                                      \ Send bit data to output                                       : SENDBIT  ( a u -- )                                             polarity @ if                                                     swap over + swap  ( index to inverted bit data )              then                                                            dup wavesiz m+!  writedata ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ PACEBIT LEADER                                                hex                                                             9 str PACEBIT  ( leader tone - 0 hz )                           ( normal )                                                      8080 , 8080 , 8080 , 8080 , 80 c,                               ( inverted )                                                    8080 , 8080 , 8080 , 8080 , 80 c,                               decimal                                                                                                                         \ Write leader                                                  : LEADER  ( -- )                                                  leadtime @  408 *  0 ?do                                          6 0 do  pacebit sendbit  loop                                 loop ;                                                                                                                                                                                        \ HIGHTONE LOWTONE                                              \ Send high tone                                                : HIGHTONE  ( -- )                                                6  speed @  /  0 do                                               sine @ if  0bit-sin  else  0bit-sqr  then  sendbit              flip-polarity                                                 loop ;                                                                                                                        \ Send low tone                                                 : LOWTONE  ( -- )                                                 6  speed @  /  0 do                                               sine @ if  1bit-sin  else  1bit-sqr  then  sendbit            loop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ 0BIT-KIM 1BIT-KIM 0BIT-SYM 1BIT-SYM                           \ Send 0-bit                                                    : 0BIT-KIM  ( -- )  hightone hightone lowtone ;                                                                                 \ Send 1-bit                                                    : 1BIT-KIM  ( -- )  hightone lowtone lowtone ;                                                                                  \ Send 0-bit                                                    : 0BIT-SYM  ( -- )                                                sine @ if  0bit-sin-sym  else  0bit-sqr-sym  then  sendbit      flip-polarity ;                                                                                                               \ Send 1-bit                                                    : 1BIT-SYM  ( -- )                                                sine @ if  1bit-sin-sym  else  1bit-sqr-sym  then  sendbit ;                                                                  \ 0BIT 1BIT SENDBYTE                                            defer 0BIT  ( -- )      \ send 0 bit                            defer 1BIT  ( -- )      \ send 1 bit                                                                                            \ Send character                                                : SENDBYTE  ( char -- )                                           sym? if  0bit  then  ( send start bit )                         0 swap  databits 0 do                                             2 /mod                                                          swap if                                                           1bit  swap 1+ swap                                            else                                                              0bit                                                          then                                                          loop 2drop ;                                                                                                                  \ STARTWAVE !SIZE                                               \ Write header, leader                                          : STARTWAVE  ( -- )                                               0. wavesiz 2!                                                   wave @  case                                                      0  of  wav-hdr writedata  endof                                 1  of  voc-hdr writedata  endof                                 endcase                                                       leader ;                                                                                                                      \ Patch WAV/VOC data size                                       : !SIZE  ( u -- )                                                 wavesiz 2@  swap  pad 2!  pad swap writedata ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ ENDWAVE                                                       \ Write leader, patch in size                                   : ENDWAVE  ( -- )                                                 leader                                                          wave @  case                                                      0  of  0 pad c!  pad 1 writedata                                       40. outfid @  reposf  4 !size                                   4.  outfid @  reposf                                            36 wavesiz m+!  4 !size  endof                           1  of  0 pad c!  pad 1 writedata                                       27. outfid @  reposf                                            2  wavesiz m+!  3 !size  endof                           endcase ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ +CHECKSUM !BYTE !WORD                                         \ Add to checksum                                               : +CHECKSUM  ( byte -- byte )                                     255 and  dup checksum +! ;                                                                                                    \ Write byte to file, bump checksum                             : !BYTE  ( u -- )                                                 +checksum  sendbyte ;                                                                                                         \ Write word (lo-hi) to file                                    : !WORD  ( u -- )                                                 0  256 um/mod  swap !byte  !byte ;            